#: manual/api/cli.md:63
msgid "a missing, repeated or unknown `--backend`, or a runner usage, file or parse error"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli.md:65
msgid "Messages go to standard output."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli.md:67
msgid "Build"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli.md:69
msgid "The executable is built by the conformance tooling:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli.md:76
msgid "`tools/conformance_cli.py` builds `src/cli` once per backend into `_build/conformance/<backend>/` and copies it to `<backend>-conformance.exe`, so parallel builds for different backends do not share a target directory."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:1
msgid "cli/gda_expr_cli API"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:5
msgid "`cli/gda_expr_cli` is the command-line runner for General Decimal Arithmetic `.decTest` corpora. It reads files, parses them with [`frontend/gda_expr`](../frontend/gda_expr.md), executes them against `decimal_gda` and prints a text or JSON summary. It is normally reached through the [`cli`](../cli.md) dispatcher as `floating-conformance --backend gda …`. See the [tutorial](../../tutorial/cli/gda_expr_cli.md) and the [design page](../../design/cli/gda_expr_cli.md)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:16
#: manual/api/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:14
#: manual/api/cli/mpfr_expr_cli.md:14
#: manual/api/cli/testfloat_expr_cli.md:15
msgid "The runner is a library, so it can be called from MoonBit code as well as through the dispatcher. Add it to the `import` block of your `moon.pkg`:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:25
msgid "The examples use the alias `@gda_expr_cli`. `run` reads files through `moonbitlang/x/fs`; the repository builds and tests the runners on the native target."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:31
#: manual/api/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:29
#: manual/api/cli/mpfr_expr_cli.md:29
#: manual/api/cli/testfloat_expr_cli.md:30
msgid "`run(arguments)` executes one invocation and returns the exit code."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:37
#: manual/api/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:35
#: manual/api/cli/testfloat_expr_cli.md:36
msgid "`arguments[0]` is the program name and is ignored. Options:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:39
#: manual/api/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:37
#: manual/api/cli/testfloat_expr_cli.md:38
msgid "Option"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:41
#: manual/api/cli/testfloat_expr_cli.md:44
msgid "print one JSON object instead of text"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:42
#: manual/api/cli/testfloat_expr_cli.md:45
msgid "`--shard-count N`, `--shard-index I` (also `=` forms)"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:42
msgid "run shard `I` of `N` (default `1`, `0`)"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:43
msgid "also fail when a selected row is unsupported or legacy"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:44
msgid "row filter: comma-separated ids or `first..last` ranges (see `RunOptions::new`)"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:45
msgid "print the usage line and return `2`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:46
msgid "`.decTest` files or directories (direct file entries ending in `.decTest`); default `testdata/decimal/smoke.decTest`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:48
msgid "Any other argument starting with `-` is an error `unknown option: …`. A directory contributes its direct file entries whose names end in `.decTest` (a directory without any adds no file); a named file without that suffix is the error `not a .decTest file: PATH`, and a path that does not exist is the error `path does not exist: PATH`, both with exit status 2. Files are sorted, each file is run once even if named twice, parsed in order (the first parse diagnostic of a file is printed as `source:line:1: message` and ends the run), and executed together, so row ordinals and shards span all files."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:57
msgid "Text output lists the counts (`cases`, `selected cases`, `executable cases`, `passed cases`, `failed cases`, `skipped cases`), the shard, and one `failed ID: MESSAGE` line per failing row. JSON output has the keys `totalCases`, `supportedCases` (executable rows), `diagnosticCases`, `legacyConditionCases`, `unsupportedCases` and an `execution` object with `executableCases`, `passedCases`, `failedCases`, `skippedCases`, `failedIds`, `shardCount`, `shardIndex`. `totalCases` counts the rows that match `--cases` in all shards; every other counter, including the top-level `supportedCases`, `diagnosticCases`, `legacyConditionCases` and `unsupportedCases`, counts only the rows of this shard. `legacyConditionCases` is always 0 with the current frontend."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:69
msgid "Return value: `2` for usage, file or parse errors; `1` when a row failed, or with `--strict-supported` when any legacy or unsupported row was selected; `0` otherwise. Diagnostic rows (`#` and `?` placeholders) never change the exit status, even with `--strict-supported`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:1
msgid "cli/itl_expr_cli API"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:5
msgid "`cli/itl_expr_cli` is the command-line runner for ITF1788 `.itl` interval test files. It parses them with [`frontend/itl_expr`](../frontend/itl_expr.md), executes every case against `ball_float` and prints a JSON report. It is normally reached as `floating-conformance --backend itl …`. See the [tutorial](../../tutorial/cli/itl_expr_cli.md) and the [design page](../../design/cli/itl_expr_cli.md)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:23
msgid "The examples use the alias `@itl_expr_cli`. `run` reads files through `moonbitlang/x/fs`; the repository builds and tests the runners on the native target."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:39
msgid "also fail when any case is unsupported"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:40
msgid "keep only cases of this operation; repeatable (cases of any listed operation are kept)"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:41
msgid "`.itl` files, read in the given order; default `testdata/interval/smoke.itl`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:43
msgid "Any other argument starting with `-` (including `--json`, `--help` and the shard options, which this runner does not have) is an error `unknown option: …`; `--operation` without a value prints `missing value for --operation`. Paths are files; directories are not expanded, and an unreadable path prints `cannot read ITL file: PATH`. Every file is parsed completely before the operation filter is applied, so a parse error in a statement of an unselected operation still ends the run: every diagnostic of that file is printed as `PATH: MESSAGE`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:52
msgid "The output is always one JSON object with the keys `schemaVersion` (`1`), `runner` (`\"itl-expression-interpreter\"`), `totalCases`, `executableCases`, `passedCases`, `failedCases`, `unsupportedCases`, `diagnosticCases`, `failedIds`, `failedMessages` (`ID: MESSAGE`), `unsupportedIds` and `diagnosticIds`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:58
msgid "Return value: `2` for usage, file or parse errors; `1` when a case failed, a case was a diagnostic, or with `--strict-supported` a case was unsupported; `0` otherwise. Cases are executed with the default precision 53."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/mpfr_expr_cli.md:1
msgid "cli/mpfr_expr_cli API"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/mpfr_expr_cli.md:5
msgid "`cli/mpfr_expr_cli` is the command-line runner for MPFR reference data. It reads one file, detects its format, parses and executes it with [`frontend/mpfr_expr`](../frontend/mpfr_expr.md) and prints a summary. It is normally reached as `floating-conformance --backend mpfr …`. See the [tutorial](../../tutorial/cli/mpfr_expr_cli.md) and the [design page](../../design/cli/mpfr_expr_cli.md)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/mpfr_expr_cli.md:23
msgid "The examples use the alias `@mpfr_expr_cli`. `run` reads files through `moonbitlang/x/fs`; the repository builds and tests the runners on the native target."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/cli/mpfr_expr_cli.md:35
msgid "`arguments[0]` is the program name and is ignored. The runner accepts `--json` and exactly one path. After `--json` is removed, any other number of arguments (none, or two or more, including shard options, which are disabled for this runner) prints `usage: mpfr-expr [--json] <MPFR sqrt, pow, or elementary corpus>`. A single remaining argument is always taken as the path, even when it starts with `-`: `--help` or a mistyped option is reported as `cannot read file: --help`. Both cases return `2`."
msgstr ""

