msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal.md:3
msgid "This tutorial shows how to compute with decimal numbers that behave the way people write them: `0.1 + 0.2` is exactly `0.3`, `12.30` remembers that it has two decimal places, and every rounding is chosen by you and reported back to you. You will parse and format values, compute under a context and read its flags, round money with `quantize`, exchange decimal64 bits, and call certified elementary functions. The mathematics behind each step is in the [decimal design](../design/decimal.md); every function is specified in the [decimal API](../api/decimal.md)."
